WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.978
Here is the HOA platform's public sample
experience, built by Catalyst

2
00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:07.241
Innovations. The communities and
information in this demonstration are

3
00:00:07.251 --> 00:00:11.592
fictional. We will follow a resident
request from the first description to

4
00:00:11.602 --> 00:00:15.580
the final review. Start by giving the
request a clear title.

5
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.931
Then describe what needs attention, so the
community team has useful context

6
00:00:19.941 --> 00:00:24.282
from the beginning. In this example, the
resident is reporting a problem

7
00:00:24.292 --> 00:00:28.270
with path lighting. Next, the form
explains what supporting information could

8
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.445
help the team understand the request.

9
00:00:30.455 --> 00:00:34.796
Clear guidance at this stage can make the
handoff easier and reduce

10
00:00:34.806 --> 00:00:36.972
the need to chase missing details.

11
00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:38.784
Continue to the review screen.

12
00:00:38.794 --> 00:00:43.135
The resident can check the information
before sending it, and go back

13
00:00:43.145 --> 00:00:47.123
if something needs changing. We are
stopping here without submitting a

14
00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:51.474
request. Sending a request does not
approve the work or reserve a

15
00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:55.825
date. This workflow gives the resident a
clear starting point and the

16
00:00:55.835 --> 00:00:57.866
community team a more structured handoff.

17
00:00:57.876 --> 00:01:01.950
Talk with Catalyst about simplifying the
everyday work in your community.

